From 76be012c00fd78ddd75b2abb4340bf7993e40fb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: indieindie7 <lonisquasar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:01:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] U2Shaders: relight (give an actor back the light its shadow
 is cast from) and borderless fullscreen

relight (on unless relight=0): Unreal II leaves a shadow's source light out when it draws the
actor (lighting it with weaker lights instead, or none), so a character under one lamp turned
black. Each shadow silhouette remembers its lights by world matrix; the actor's lit main-view
draws get any missing one turned on in a free slot for that draw.

fakefull.hpp: a fullscreen request becomes a windowed device and the window a frameless popup over
the monitor, restyled inside CreateDevice/Reset with the size messages kept from the game (the old
watcher-thread resize aborted). fullscreen=exclusive in U2Shaders.ini keeps real fullscreen.
Tested in Unreal II without dgVoodoo (system d3d9): 1920x1080 borderless, vsync, PCSS, post.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
